  "worked_solution": "Recall that the graph of an odd function must have rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin.\n\n- Graphs II, III, and IV do not have rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. So, it is **not** an odd function.\n\n- On the other hand, graph I does have rotational symmetry about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that graph  I  show odd functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246337/assets/3b5e234a3416a5e7100468b81f170171a873508eb0c87bba126009daca9e49bc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
