  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-110654\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Recall that the graph of an odd function must have rotational symmetry of order <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"39\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> about the origin.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Graphs II, III, and IV do not have rotational symmetry of order <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"40\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> about the origin. So, it is <strong>not</strong> an odd function.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>On the other hand, graph I does have rotational symmetry about the origin. If we rotate the graph <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"41\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.393em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that graph  I  show odd functions.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-110654-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-110654-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"</p>\n</div>",
